  "status": "beta",
  "statement": "Find the last two digits of $3^{2026}$.",
  "answer_format": "integer_0_999",
  "answer_hash": "10df797c",
  "hints": [
    "Find the smallest $m$ with $3^m \\equiv 1 \\pmod{100}$. Start from $3^4 = 81$."
  ],
  "solution": "$81^2 \\equiv 61$, $81^4 \\equiv 21$ and $81^5 \\equiv 21\\cdot 81 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{100}$, so $3^{20}\\equiv 1$. Since $2026 = 20\\cdot 101 + 6$, we get $3^{2026}\\equiv 3^6 = 729 \\equiv 29$.",
